.TH "libnvmf_import_tls_key_versioned" 9 "libnvmf_import_tls_key_versioned" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_import_tls_key_versioned \- Decode a PSK from the PSK interchange format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_import_tls_key_versioned
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *encoded_key "  ","
.BI "unsigned char *version "  ","
.BI "enum libnvmf_hmac_alg *hmac "  ","
.BI "size_t *key_len "  ","
.BI "unsigned char **key "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
struct libnvme_global_ctx object
.IP "encoded_key" 12
PSK in PSK interchange format
.IP "version" 12
Version of the PSK interchange format read from
\fIencoded_key\fP to return. Always 1; any other value
is rejected with -EINVAL.
.IP "hmac" 12
Hash function recorded in \fIencoded_key\fP to return; it
derives a retained PSK from a configured PSK
.IP "key_len" 12
Length of the decoded PSK to return
.IP "key" 12
Decoded PSK to return
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Decodes \fIencoded_key\fP from the PSK Interchange format as defined in
section 3.6.1.5 of the NVMe TCP Transport Specification 1.3.

It is the responsibility of the caller to free the returned buffer.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, negative error code otherwise.
